diff --git a/crates/rightkit-models/CHANGELOG.md b/crates/rightkit-models/CHANGELOG.md
index 5cbb2c8b..b560a41f 100644
--- a/crates/rightkit-models/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/crates/rightkit-models/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -2,6 +2,13 @@
 
 ## Unreleased
 
+- **Breaking for tests that relied on the real per-user default: under test, the real folder is refused.** No test may read or write a real user's data, so every resolver whose default is the real per-user folder now refuses while the process is under test. A process is under test when `RIGHTKIT_UNDER_TEST` is set to a non-empty value other than `0`, or when its executable sits in a Cargo `deps` or `examples` directory under a `target` profile directory (`.../target/<profile>/deps/<exe>`, `.../<target-dir>/<triple>/<profile>/deps/<exe>`; the program directly in `<profile>/`, as with `cargo run`, is not a test). Installed apps and dev runs are unaffected. An override (`RIGHT_SUITE_DIR`, `ORTHIC_SHARED_DIR`) or an explicit root always wins, except that under test an override pointing into the real `<data>/Orthic Labs` or `<data>/RightSuite` folder is refused too.
+  - Panic (the function cannot return an error without a signature change, and a silent temp folder or an empty result would hide the fault): `suite::paths::{suite_root, legacy_suite_root, models_root, tools_root}`, `ModelStore::shared`, `suite::handle::sibling_parakeet_dirs`, `suite::discover::find_existing_elsewhere`, `suite::lease::current_holder`. The message names the resolver, says the process is under test and names `RIGHT_SUITE_DIR`.
+  - Error: `suite::device_id_get_or_create` and `suite::lease::try_acquire_compat` (`Err(String)`), `ModelStore::resolve_parakeet` (`Err(String)`), `suite::paths::shared_runtime_dir`, `suite::whisper::{resolve_whisper_model, ensure_whisper_model}` (the new `ErrorCode::UnderTest`).
+  - Comparisons with the shared store inside `ModelStore::resolve`, `ensure_ready*`, `migrate_*`, `prune_unref_entries*`, `try_acquire_for_gc` and `readiness_report_at` no longer resolve the real folder for a store at an explicit root: under test without an override the explicit root is simply "not the shared one".
+  - `ErrorCode` gains `UnderTest` (an exhaustive `match` needs an arm).
+  - Existing test changed: `tests/suite_paths.rs` asserted the real default (`<data>/Orthic Labs/shared`); it now asserts the refusal. New: `tests/under_test.rs`, and unit tests in `suite/{paths,handle,install,discover}.rs` through seams that take the flag and data directory as parameters.
+
 - `http::ModelHttpOptions` gains, all additive with the previous behaviour as the default (`ModelHttpOptions` is built with `..Default::default()` in every caller in this repository; a struct literal without it needs the new fields):
   - `trust: TrustRoots` (default `Platform`, the operating system's store; `Bundled` is `rightkit-http`'s Mozilla set). `TrustRoots`, `HttpError` and `DEFAULT_RETRIES` are exported from `http`. `rightkit-http` has no caller-supplied-roots option, so an app's own roots are not possible here.
   - `header_timeout: Option<Duration>` (default 60 s, which `rightkit-http` already applied; it is now settable). The existing `connect_timeout` (30 s) and `read_timeout` (the idle limit, 120 s) are unchanged.
