 - **Licence.** To be confirmed. The existing specs in this catalog carry no licence field, and
   none was sourced for this bundle.
 
+## Under test
+
+No test may read or write a real user's data, so every resolver whose default is the real per-user folder refuses while the process is under test.
+
+- **Under test** means `RIGHTKIT_UNDER_TEST` is set to a non-empty value other than `0`, or the executable's path has a parent directory named `deps` or `examples` whose parent chain is a Cargo target profile: `.../target/<profile>/deps/<exe>` or `.../<target-dir>/<triple>/<profile>/deps/<exe>`. The program directly in `<profile>/` (`cargo run`, a dev build) is not a test. The path rule cannot be switched off.
+- **Panics** (infallible signatures; a silent temp folder or empty result would hide the fault): `suite::paths::{suite_root, legacy_suite_root, models_root, tools_root}` unless `RIGHT_SUITE_DIR` (or, for all but the legacy root, `ORTHIC_SHARED_DIR`) names a folder; `ModelStore::shared`; `suite::handle::sibling_parakeet_dirs` and `suite::discover::find_existing_elsewhere` (no override exists: pass explicit directories to `ModelStore::resolve`, or use `find_existing_under`); `suite::lease::current_holder`.
+- **Returns an error:** `suite::device_id_get_or_create` (use `device_id_in`), `suite::lease::try_acquire_compat`, `ModelStore::resolve_parakeet` (`Err(String)`); `suite::paths::shared_runtime_dir` and `suite::whisper::{resolve_whisper_model, ensure_whisper_model}` (`ErrorCode::UnderTest`).
+- **Never refused:** an override variable that names a folder outside the real one, and every `*_at` / explicit-root function (`ModelStore::at_models_root`, `models_root_at`, `device_id_in`, `find_existing_under`, ...). Under test an override that points into the real `<data>/Orthic Labs` or `<data>/RightSuite` folder is refused too.
+- **Unaffected:** installed apps and `cargo run`. A store at an explicit root is simply not "the shared store" for the internal comparisons, so no test needs a variable to use `at_models_root`.
+
 ## Wrapping this crate
 
 An app that wraps the suite crate (a shared-store wrapper or a host SDK) re-exports the
@@ -195,7 +205,7 @@ use rightkit_models::{EntitlementError, ModelStore};
 use rightkit_models::suite::catalog::ModelSpec; // the suite's catalog spec, not the root `ModelSpec`
 ```
 
-- `ModelStore::shared(app_id)` binds the machine-wide shared store (`ORTHIC_SHARED_DIR` overrides its root); `ModelStore::at_models_root(root, app_id)`
+- `ModelStore::shared(app_id)` binds the machine-wide shared store (`RIGHT_SUITE_DIR` or `ORTHIC_SHARED_DIR` overrides its root; it panics under test without one, see "Under test"); `ModelStore::at_models_root(root, app_id)`
   binds an explicit directory (tests, sandboxes). `with_http_client` swaps the transport.
 - `EntitlementError` is what `try_ensure_entitled` returns. Match on it to tell "not entitled"
   (`NotEntitled`), "back off" (`RateLimited`), "retry" (`Transport`) and "local failure" (`Install`).
